36,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"Good morning, everyone! I hope you all had sweet dreams! I'm so curious—did our Seer find any big clues last night? Does anyone want to share what they know, or should we just keep observing?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"Good morning. As we discussed, the Seer's information is our most valuable asset, but revealing it too early is a risk. I believe we should first see if anyone has noticed any suspicious patterns in our behavior.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,1,1,talk,Toshio,,"I agree with Victoria. We should not pressure the Seer to reveal themselves prematurely. Instead, let us analyze the current atmosphere. Does anyone feel that someone's tone has shifted since yesterday?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,1,1,talk,George,,"I have not noticed any significant shifts in tone yet. However, I am curious if anyone feels a sudden urge to lead the group's direction today. Let us be careful not to rush our judgments.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,1,1,talk,Sakura,,"I'm awake! Hehe! I wonder if the Seer found a big, scary wolf already? @everyone, does anyone feel like they're acting a little bit different today? I'm watching you all very closely with my spy eyes!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Victoria, @Toshio, @George, you're all still so calm! It's almost spooky! @Sakura, I don't think anyone's acting different yet, but maybe the wolf is just really good at pretending! Does anyone have a gut feeling?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Toshio"",""George"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Kenji, gut feelings are often misleading in a game designed for deception. I prefer to rely on evidence. However, I can say that George's consistent composure is noted, though not necessarily suspicious. What about you, @Toshio?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""George"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, I share your view on gut feelings. While George is consistent, consistency can be a mask. I am more interested in how the others react to the silence of the Seer. Is anyone becoming impatient?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,1,2,talk,George,,"@Toshio, impatience is often a sign of desperation. I find the current silence quite natural. Rather than searching for a mask, perhaps we should consider who benefits most from a prolonged stalemate.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"@George, that's a super-smart question! Hehe! Maybe the wolf is just sitting back and laughing while we all wonder who's the bad guy! That would be a really mean trick! Who do you think is the most patient person here?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, that's a scary thought! I don't want the wolf to be laughing at us! I think @George and @Toshio are the most patient. But wait, does being patient make you suspicious? I'm so confused!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""George"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Kenji, patience is not a crime, but it can be a strategy. The key is whether that patience is used to observe or to hide. @George, you mentioned the benefit of a stalemate; do you have a specific suspect in mind?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@George, your question about who benefits from a stalemate is a sharp one. Usually, the werewolf and the possessed prefer a slow pace to avoid early mistakes. I am watching to see who steers us toward inaction.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,1,3,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I am merely posing a question for the group's consideration, not steering us toward inaction. I believe we should be wary of those who use logic as a shield to avoid giving any concrete opinions.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"@George, you're so fancy with your words! Hehe! But wait, if we're all just using logic as shields, then we're all just a bunch of turtles! Maybe the wolf is the one who's being the most ""logical"" to trick us! Who's the most logical person here?","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, turtles! Hehe, that's funny! I think @Victoria and @Toshio are the most logical. But if Sakura is right, that means they could be the wolf! Oh no, now I'm even more confused! Who should we vote for?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Victoria"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Kenji, please do not let Sakura's playful analogies confuse you. Logic is a tool, not a mask. However, we must decide. Since no one has claimed Seer, I suggest we look at who has been most deflective.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,1,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, I agree. Deflection is a key indicator. While we have no concrete evidence, I find the lack of a Seer's claim concerning. If the Seer is among us, their silence is a risk; if not, we are blind. I suggest we vote cautiously.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,1,4,talk,George,,"I believe we should avoid a rash decision based on mere suspicion. However, if we must vote, let us consider if anyone has been too eager to cast doubt on others without providing evidence. I will reserve my final choice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,1,4,talk,Sakura,,"Hmm, this is so hard! Everyone is being so careful! Hehe, but @Victoria and @Toshio are acting like a team of super-serious detectives! Maybe they're just really smart, or maybe they're the wolf! I'll just follow my spy instincts!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
